# Kapri — Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your keys.
# The app works without any keys (Tier 3 scripted engine),
# but live Kapruka data requires at least ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.

# ─── Tier 1: Anthropic (recommended) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Used for: claude-sonnet-4-6 + Kapruka MCP via Anthropic's MCP beta proxy.
# The Anthropic SDK routes MCP calls through Anthropic's servers, which are
# IP-allowlisted by mcp.kapruka.com — so this works from any environment.
# Get your key at: https://console.anthropic.com/settings/api-keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ─── Tier 2: Google Gemini (optional fallback) ─────────────────────────────────
# Used for: gemini-2.5-flash via @ai-sdk/mcp direct HTTP to mcp.kapruka.com.
# Only called if Tier 1 fails or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is not set.
# Get your key at: https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=

# ─── Notes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# • NEVER prefix these with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — they must stay server-side only.
# • Tier 3 (scripted engine) requires no keys and always works as a final fallback.
# • On Vercel: set these in Project Settings → Environment Variables.
# • Rate limits: 60 req/min across all Kapruka tools; 30 create_order/hour.
